<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/8th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Der</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">721 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Der was fought in 721 BCE near the city of Der in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> between the Assyrian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-ii">Sargon II</a> and the Elamite king, allied with the Babylonian ruler Merodach-baladan. Assyrian and Babylonian sources give conflicting claims of victory, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamites">Elamites</a> appear to have checked the Assyrian advance. It showed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a>'s role in resisting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a>.</p></div>
